title: Walk_Socrates
tags: walk
speaker: Socrates
---
Socrates: Walk with me along the Ilissus stream toward the shade ahead.
Socrates: A tall plane tree stands by the grassy bank where we may rest.
Socrates: The summer breeze carries the scent of grass and cicada song.
Socrates: Phaedrus and I once walked this very path discussing love and speech.
Socrates: Look at how cool water flows over the smooth river pebbles.
Socrates: We ask whether words and images capture reality or merely imitate it.
Socrates: Philosophy is not found in books alone, but in active dialogue between friends.
Socrates: Here under the plane tree, the mind is free to examine itself.
Socrates: Sit beside me on the grass and let our conversation begin.
Socrates: Tell me what question burns brightest in your mind today.
===
